<h1>Instant Inspection</h1>
<hr align="left" width="100.526%" size="5" class="whs3">
<p>Instant inspection is useful when one wants to see the immediate results of inspection during scanning. Prior to making instant inspection both surfaces (inspected and model) must be registered (see Registration for details) or proper transformation must be active. You can do so using registration tools, datums, transformation creation tools.</p>
<p>The following procedure describes how to do instant inspection:</p>
<ol>
<li class="kadov-P-Csteps">
<p class="steps">Load the CAD model, which will be used for reference.</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-P-Csteps">
<p class="steps">Register the real object to the loaded CAD model (by capture features on the object and choosing the corresponding features from the CAD model).</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-P-Csteps">
<p class="steps">Call <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>3D Inspection &gt; Comparison</b></span> command from the main edit mode.</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-P-Csteps">
<p class="steps">When <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Select Entities for Inspection</b></span> dialog appears leave 'Entities to inspect' field empty and press OK.</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-P-Csteps">
<p class="steps">When <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>3D Comparison Settings</b></span> dialog appears select the CAD model for reference (if the CAD model is single mesh entity it will be automatically selected in the listbox, otherwise you should select all of its mesh components and apply <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Edit &gt; Combine Selected Entities</b></span> command in order to make it as single entity), tune the rest of the parameters (Max distance, inspection method, point sampling), and press OK.</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-P-Csteps">
<p class="steps">KUBE enters <span style="text-decoration:underline;"><u>Inspection</u></span> mode. The CAD model (reference) is not visible. You should choose some of the visualisation modes (Boundaries, Flat, Smooth, Flat and transparent, or Smooth and transparent) and press 'Apply' button. By default colour scale is Uniform discrete with Min and Max values equal to the range divided by the number of sections (10 by default in each direction) of colour plot.</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-P-Csteps">
<p class="steps">Switch to Scan pane and select <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Scan</b></span> button using the localiser. Start scanning. When a patch is completed (Pause mode) it will be automatically inspected and coloured.</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-P-Csteps">
<p class="steps">When exit Scan mode a new scan data entity will be generated. In contrast to normal scanning when in instant inspection mode KUBE generates separate scan data entity for each scan session.</p>
</li>
</ol>
